    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n72702" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἶτος</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>fate, doom,</i> usu. in a bad
			sense, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κακὸς οἶ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					8.34
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				1.350
			</span></i>, al.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σὺ δέ κεν κακὸν οἶ. ὄληαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					3.417
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλκυόνος πολυπενθέος οἶ. ἔχουσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					9.563
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καλὰ τὸν οἶ. ἀπότμου παιδὸς ἔνισπες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					24.388
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατὰ κόσμον Ἀχαιῶν οἶ. ἀείδεις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					8.489
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δαναῶν ἰδὲ Ἰλίου οἶ.
				ἀκούων</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				578
			</span></i> ; but simply, <i>lot,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν τῆς μελίσσης οἶ. ἔχειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Democr.
					227
				</span></i>
			.—
				Ep.
			 word, used in lyr. by <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>El.</u>
				167
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>IT</u>
				1091
			</span></i> (dub. l.). (Prob. from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἶμι</span>
			<i>ibo.</i>)</div>
